      "math_academy_id": "e-8462",
      "problem": "Given that $X \\sim U \\left\\lbrace 7, 8, 9, \\ldots, 21 \\right\\rbrace,$ compute $P(X = 18).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14268989/assets/409e0861b10e01378bf2d4daec78c5689ab622157c841d6da4ee528ac7dc63e4.svg)\n\nHere, we have $X \\sim U \\left\\lbrace 7, 8, 9, \\ldots, 21 \\right\\rbrace,$ and the set $S = \\left\\lbrace 7, 8, 9, \\ldots, 21 \\right\\rbrace$ has $|S|=21 - 7 + 1 = 15$ items. So, we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14268989/assets/41d85a92f23118e823cb96c15d6a347036f758ebb8a14c695384755da253b380.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X = 18) = f(18) = \\dfrac{1}{15}.\n$$",
